Now the big one: BatchService. Changes:

1. `createBatch`: validate recipe binding; extend fingerprint; insert with new fields; response includes new fields.
2. `approve`: add release gate before insertApproval when newStatus == RELEASED and recipe bound.
3. `split`: inheritance logic; child BatchRow with new fields; SplitChild with targetMassGrams.
4. `toBatchResponse`: new fields.
5. New methods at end: createRecipe, weigh, correctWeighing, weighingChain, plus private helpers (effectiveTotals, assertRecipeMetForRelease, validateAmount, etc.).
6. fingerprint: switch to structured length-prefix encoding.
7. New command type constants.

Also BatchRow constructor calls in createBatch and split need the 3 extra args.

Let me carefully make the edits via PowerShell replacements. Since the file has Chinese comments (mojibake in console but actual UTF-8), my anchors must match exact text. ASCII-only anchors are safest.

Edit 1 — constants:
```java
    private static final String CMD_SPLIT = "SPLIT";
```
add new constants after.

Edit 2 — fingerprint method: replace body. Current:
```java
    private String fingerprint(String... parts) {        String canonical = String.join(SEP, parts);
```
Note the weird formatting (the `{` followed by spaces and statement on same line). I'll replace the whole method. Anchor: "private String fingerprint(String... parts)" through the closing of method. The method body:

```java
    private String fingerprint(String... parts) {        String canonical = String.join(SEP, parts);
        try {
            MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            ...
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 ...", e);
        }
    }
```

I'll replace from "private String fingerprint" up to "    }\n\n    /**\n     * 拆分" — hard with Chinese. Alternative: replace just the first line `String canonical = String.join(SEP, parts);` with structured building. The line is:

`    private String fingerprint(String... parts) {        String canonical = String.join(SEP, parts);`

Replace with:

```java
    private String fingerprint(String... parts) {
        // 结构化拼接：每段带长度前缀，避免分隔符碰撞；null 归一为空串
        StringBuilder canonical = new StringBuilder();
        for (String part : parts) {
            String value = part == null ? "" : part;
            canonical.append(value.length()).append(':').append(value);
        }
```

and then `digest.digest(canonical.getBytes(...))` → `canonical.toString().getBytes(...)`. There's a line `byte[] hash = digest.digest(canonical.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));` → replace `canonical.getBytes` with `canonical.toString().getBytes`.

Also SEP constant becomes unused — remove it or keep? Unused private constant → javac doesn't warn as error. Remove to be clean. The SEP declaration has a Chinese comment above it. Anchor:

```
    private static final String SEP = "\u0000";
```
The file literally contains `"\u0000"`? In Java source it's written as `"\u0000"` escape — 6 chars. Yes. Remove that line and its comment. The comment line above is Chinese; I can remove just the SEP line (leaving comment orphaned — bad). Let me find the comment text: "指纹拼接分隔符（NUL）：业务参数不可能包含该字符，避免拼接碰撞。" I'll replace the whole block using regex. Simpler: replace the SEP line with nothing and also remove the preceding comment lines via regex matching `/**...*/\n    private static final String SEP...`. PowerShell regex with Singleline. Let me do:

```powershell
$t = [regex]::Replace($t, '(?s)\s*/\*\*.*?\*/\s*private static final String SEP = "\\u0000";', '')
```

Careful with escaping in PowerShell string — use single-quoted PS string, regex: `\s*/\*\*.*?\*/\s*private static final String SEP = "\\u0000";` — in regex, `\\u0000` matches literal backslash-u0000? In .NET regex, `\\` matches a literal backslash, then `u0000` literal. Good.

Edit 3 — createBatch. Current relevant code:

```java
    public StoredResponse createBatch(CreateBatchRequest req) {
        List<String> items = req.requiredTests().stream().map(String::trim).toList();
        if (new HashSet<>(items).size() != items.size()) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest("requiredTests 存在重复检验项");
        }
        String fingerprint = fingerprint("create", req.batchKey(), req.productCode(), req.batchNo(),
                req.producedAt().toString(), String.join(SEP, items));
```

`String.join(SEP, items)` — SEP removed; replace with `String.join(",", items)`? For structured fingerprint, join items with length-prefix... simplest: pass items joined by "," — collision risk between item lists like ["a,b"] vs ["a","b"]. To stay structured, I can build fingerprint parts list: parts = ["create", batchKey, productCode, batchNo, producedAt, recipeKey, targetMass, item1...itemN]. Since fingerprint() now length-prefixes each part, passing items as separate varargs is fully structured. 

New code:

```java
    public StoredResponse createBatch(CreateBatchRequest req) {
        List<String> items = req.requiredTests().stream().map(String::trim).toList();
        if (new HashSet<>(items).size() != items.size()) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest("requiredTests 存在重复检验项");
        }
        boolean bindRecipe = req.recipeKey() != null || req.targetMassGrams() != null;
        if (bindRecipe && (req.recipeKey() == null || req.recipeKey().isBlank()
                || req.targetMassGrams() == null)) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest("绑定配方时 recipeKey 与 targetMassGrams 必须同时提供");
        }
        if (bindRecipe) {
            requireMass(req.targetMassGrams(), "targetMassGrams");
        }
        List<String> parts = new ArrayList<>(List.of("create", req.batchKey(), req.productCode(),
                req.batchNo(), req.producedAt().toString(),
                req.recipeKey() == null ? "" : req.recipeKey().trim(),
                req.targetMassGrams() == null ? "" : req.targetMassGrams().toPlainString()));
        parts.addAll(items);
        String fingerprint = fingerprint(parts.toArray(new String[0]));
        return executeIdempotent(CMD_CREATE, req.commandKey(), fingerprint, () -> {
            repo.findBatch(req.batchKey()).ifPresent(b -> {
                throw ApiException.conflict("batchKey 已存在: " + req.batchKey());
            });
            String recipeKey = null;
            if (bindRecipe) {
                recipeKey = req.recipeKey().trim();
                if (repo.findRecipe(recipeKey).isEmpty()) {
                    throw ApiException.unprocessable("配方版本不存在: " + recipeKey);
                }
            }
            String now = now();
            repo.insertBatch(new BatchRepository.BatchRow(0L, req.batchKey(), req.productCode(),
                    req.batchNo(), req.producedAt().toString(), BatchStatus.QUARANTINED.name(), now,
                    recipeKey, req.targetMassGrams(), 0));
            for (int i = 0; i < items.size(); i++) {
                repo.insertRequiredTest(req.batchKey(), items.get(i), i + 1);
            }
            BatchResponse body = new BatchResponse(req.batchKey(), req.productCode(), req.batchNo(),
                    req.producedAt(), BatchStatus.QUARANTINED, items, Instant.parse(now),
                    recipeKey, req.targetMassGrams());
            return new StoredResponse(201, toJson(body));
        });
    }
```

Wait — requireMass for targetMass: positive + ≤6 decimals + bound. I'll write helper:

```java
    private void requireMass(BigDecimal value, String field) {
        if (value.signum() <= 0) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest(field + " 必须为正值");
        }
        if (value.stripTrailingZeros().scale() > 6) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest(field + " 最多6位小数");
        }
        if (value.compareTo(MAX_MASS) > 0) {
            throw ApiException.badRequest(field + " 超出可表示范围");
        }
    }
```

MAX_MASS = new BigDecimal("9999999999999.999999")? DECIMAL(19,6): 13 integer digits. Max = 9999999999999.999999. OK.

Note: validation of targetMass should happen before idempotency (so failures don't occupy key — actually failures never occupy key since command_log only written on success; validation inside or outside tx both fine. But "失败不占键" holds either way).

Edit 4 — approve gate. In approve(), after computing seq/newStatus, before insertApproval:

```java
            if (newStatus == BatchStatus.RELEASED && batch.recipeKey() != null) {
                assertRecipeMetForRelease(batch);
            }
```

Edit 5 — split. Current child creation:

```java
            String now = now();
            List<String> required = repo.findRequiredTests(parentKey);
